{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/846958-how-does-a-human-become-a-beast","id":846958,"title":"How does a human become a Beast?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Beast: The Primordial"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-03-14T00:18:41-07:00","id":846958,"title":"How does a human become a Beast?","content":"I've been reading the Preview and I've been trying to understand how a human becomes a Beast. It is from a dream like state if understand correctly. And is it possible to rp out a story in which the characters start human and become Beast? How would it work?<br /> <br /> Sorry for the silly questions, I'm new to Onyx Path, and have many questions of the path of Beast <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Thanks in advance!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11457-volke","name":"Volke","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11457_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"127"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-14T00:31:37-07:00","id":846959,"title":"","content":"A character who becomes a Beast has nightmares that touch a foundational part of the collective human unconscious, somewhere in the borderland between the animal survival instincts of the species and the formless dream-creatures whose psychic domain can influence the physical world. At some point, the character recognizes that the recurring presence in these nightmares of theirs was their Primordial Self, at which point they Devour themselves and become the monster within the nightmare.<br /> <br /> It's definitely possible to run an extended prelude sort of story.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-14T07:13:30-07:00","id":847054,"title":"","content":"Wait, wasn't there a Mythos or legend mechanic in Beast? If so, would that technically mean these people are reincarnations of bygone Beasts? Or are Beasts innately immortal? I forget...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>nWoD Warhammer Fantasy RPG,<br /> WoD Wraith: The Oblivion<br /> and Infernum-style Demon: The Descent, Shadows of Abaddon --&gt; <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php/topic,26.0.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://madnessforums.com/forums/inde...opic,26.0.html</a><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","name":"MrParaduo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar974_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"967"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-14T08:09:13-07:00","id":847079,"title":"","content":"By default beasts are long-lived but not immortal. Whether or not beast's horrors reincarnate between hosts is a little fuzzy, even in-game, not least because at that level of the astral everyone sort of shares one big soul.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-14T08:15:05-07:00","id":847087,"title":"","content":"Beasts aren't inherently immortal, but having a high Lair increases one's lifespan. Incarnate Beasts, I believe, are immortal, while the Unfettered are ephemeral entities and so their existences are not dependent on the necessities of biology. The possibility of reincarnation is never touched on in Beast, but it's certainly an interesting idea and probably gets bandied about in Begotten communities (although probably runs into the same problems Sin-Eaters have when two different Beasts whose Horrors both appear to be Akkorokamui or Medusa run into each other).<br /> <br /> Edit: Ninja'd by Elfive. Life's one big miracle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-14T09:02:49-07:00","id":847108,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrParaduo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/846958-how-does-a-human-become-a-beast?p=847054#post847054\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wait, wasn't there a Mythos or legend mechanic in Beast? If so, would that technically mean these people are reincarnations of bygone Beasts? Or are Beasts innately immortal? I forget...</div> </div> </div> </div>Legend and Life are the Virtue/Vice analogues (Mythos is something they can accrue later on as part of an endgame). That said, there are cases where a Beast's Horror is believed to have existed since ancient times. It doesn't have mechanical representation, but could be a matter of reincarnation (a Horror connected to Beast after Beast), Horrors copying traits from predecessors, Horrors spawning offspring (those last two would make the Horror younger, but explain why it resembled an older one), or a Horror that's only just now gained a Beast that's tied to it (what stopped it before?). Unless it's been clarified in a later version that I've seen, it's a murky area.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-14T10:02:14-07:00","id":847154,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>espritdecalmar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/846958-how-does-a-human-become-a-beast?p=847087#post847087\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(although probably runs into the same problems Sin-Eaters have when two different Beasts whose Horrors both appear to be Akkorokamui or Medusa run into each other).</div> </div> </div> </div>One advantage to literally being the human face of a nightmare creature from before human language is that you can be pretty sure the other inchoate mirror-serpent is not you regardless of what either of you is called.<br /> <br /> The Bound run into that problem because they interact with entities that more commonly deal with masks and memory at some number of removes. A Horror doesn't choose to look like a gashadokuro because it's convenient.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-14T10:16:29-07:00","id":847164,"title":"","content":"I'm having trouble remembering the difference between the Homecoming and the Devouring.<br /> <br /> I think the former happens while the human is awake, and the process is assisted by other Beasts who explain the situation and welcome the new family member. <br /> <br /> The latter is more solitary and happens in dreams, usually culminating in the Horror actually eating the dreaming human in some way, making them wake up as a Beast.<br /> <br /> Am I right?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 03-14-2016, 01:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-14T10:24:09-07:00","id":847173,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/846958-how-does-a-human-become-a-beast?p=847154#post847154\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One advantage to literally being the human face of a nightmare creature from before human language is that you can be pretty sure the other inchoate mirror-serpent is not you regardless of what either of you is called.<br /> <br /> The Bound run into that problem because they interact with entities that more commonly deal with masks and memory at some number of removes. A Horror doesn't choose to look like a gashadokuro because it's convenient.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's fair. I wonder if there are any Begotten who put the cart before the horse and think that their Horror is literally a specific monster from myth. Retreading Sacrosanct territory is probably unnecessary, but it could make for an interesting conflict, especially if an Apex (or Apex-aspiring) is involved.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-14T10:28:03-07:00","id":847176,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GottaGoFeast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/846958-how-does-a-human-become-a-beast?p=847164#post847164\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm having trouble remembering the difference between the Homecoming and the Devouring.<br /> <br /> I think the former happens while the human is awake, and the process is assisted by other Beasts who explain the situation and welcome the new family member.<br /> <br /> The latter is more solitary and happens in dreams, usually culminating in the Horror actually eating the dreaming human in some way, making them wake up as a Beast.<br /> <br /> Am I right?</div> </div> </div> </div>The only difference between the Homecoming and the Devouring is that the Devouring is sometimes preceded by the dream-eating of the new Beast's human soul by their elder sibling.<br /> <br /> Either way, the character knowingly allows themselves to be consumed by a Horror as the gateway to becoming one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-14T10:52:18-07:00","id":847194,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/846958-how-does-a-human-become-a-beast?p=846959#post846959\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A character who becomes a Beast has nightmares that touch a foundational part of the collective human unconscious, somewhere in the borderland between the animal survival instincts of the species and the formless dream-creatures whose psychic domain can influence the physical world. At some point, the character recognizes that the recurring presence in these nightmares of theirs was their Primordial Self, at which point they Devour themselves and become the monster within the nightmare.<br /> <br /> It's definitely possible to run an extended prelude sort of story.</div> </div> </div> </div>So in this case Satchel, how would that work exactly? Can another Beast force a mortal to become a Beast if it needs to be a solitary process? Or would the only possible way would be with a Mythic self? The whole process has me confused. I understand that they eventually conquer their nightmares to become Beasts themselves<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11457-volke","name":"Volke","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11457_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"127"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-14T11:10:59-07:00","id":847203,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Volke</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/846958-how-does-a-human-become-a-beast?p=847194#post847194\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can another Beast force a mortal to become a Beast if it needs to be a solitary process? Or would the only possible way would be with a Mythic self? The whole process has me confused.</div> </div> </div> </div>You can't really force the prerequisite connection to the Primordial Dream. The Devouring can and does happen with the involvement of another Beast, but that's largely a matter of giving the dreamer room for the seed of their Lair to take root. It's not a process that can be initiated for anyone and everyone who doesn't have a supernatural template.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I understand that they eventually conquer their nightmares to become Beasts themselves </div> </div> </div>It's more like embracing their nightmares than conquering them, really. They're making a deeper connection rather than asserting dominion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-14T11:15:01-07:00","id":847205,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/846958-how-does-a-human-become-a-beast?p=847203#post847203\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can't really force the prerequisite connection to the Primordial Dream. The Devouring can and does happen with the involvement of another Beast, but that's largely a matter of giving the dreamer room for the seed of their Lair to take root. It's not a process that can be initiated for anyone and everyone who doesn't have a supernatural template.<br /> <br /> It's more like embracing their nightmares than conquering them, really. They're making a deeper connection rather than asserting dominion.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Now by supernatural template what do you mean: I thought Beasts were humans that felt a connection to the Primordial Dream. I understand about embracing nightmares, I just wonder how it would all work to a mortal to Beast campaign. That's what I have wanted to do but am unsure how I would make it work - I apologize. I'm new to WOD and the Beast in general, I still haven't finished the book - but I really appreciate yours and everyone's responses so far <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> . Thank you. But if you can help me make sense of this would be great <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11457-volke","name":"Volke","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11457_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"127"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-14T11:23:48-07:00","id":847212,"title":"","content":"Not having a supernatural template is a rules way of saying not already some other kind of supernatural. So not any and every human can become a Beast, only someone who's already a Beast-in-waiting by virtue of their connection to the Primordial Dream.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-14T11:27:27-07:00","id":847217,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Volke</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/846958-how-does-a-human-become-a-beast?p=847205#post847205\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now by supernatural template what do you mean: I thought Beasts were humans that felt a connection to the Primordial Dream.</div> </div> </div> </div>Beasts were humans with a connection to the Primordial Dream prior to the Devouring; after they reconcile their Mythic Self with their waking life they are more properly residents of the Dream with a human life and history.<br /> <br /> By &quot;supernatural template&quot; I basically just mean that the usual rule of thumb for supernatural beings in the Chronicles of Darkness about vampirism/lycanthropy/enlightenment/etc being mutually exclusive states in general also applies to Beasts \u2014 in the context of the whole sentence, I'm saying that just like not just anybody becomes a werewolf or a changeling or a Sin-Eater, the Begotten can't reliably and deliberately increase their population without suitable people who can become that type of monster.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-14T11:51:14-07:00","id":847225,"title":"","content":"Basically you can think of becoming a beast as falling off a cliff. You can either jump or be pushed, but you need a cliff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-14T12:10:31-07:00","id":847232,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/846958-how-does-a-human-become-a-beast?p=847225#post847225\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Basically you can think of becoming a beast as falling off a cliff. You can either jump or be pushed, but you need a cliff.</div> </div> </div> </div>Expanding this metaphor: Is there any way to carve out a cliff by oneself?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11117-inquisitor","name":"Inquisitor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11117_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"138"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-14T12:14:12-07:00","id":847234,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Inquisitor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/846958-how-does-a-human-become-a-beast?p=847232#post847232\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Expanding this metaphor: Is there any way to carve out a cliff by oneself?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not as such I don't think. One is either born with a connection to the Dream or not. That kind of stuff is plot-device shenanigans although it might be within the abilities of an Incarnate. It would depend on the Storyteller.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-14T12:53:56-07:00","id":847245,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Inquisitor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/846958-how-does-a-human-become-a-beast?p=847232#post847232\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Expanding this metaphor: Is there any way to carve out a cliff by oneself?</div> </div> </div> </div>In real life, the answer is yes. We've seen it done, but it largely takes a lifetime.<br /> <br /> Does this mean a person can build the metaphysical infrastructure needed to become a Beast? The answer to that is <i>maaaaybe</i>, but you would need someone who knew what was going on, knew how to affect it within the limits of their mortality, had the desire to do it, and the dedication to do it. And all of that would probably still take a lifetime.<br /> <br /> So really, the answer's no. Maybe one in a millenium does it, and I can't see it benefiting them much in their old age, in fact it probably leads to them dying soon after that. Which is in someways appropriate to Beast's themes. Mankind is capable of great things, but it's not as capable as the forces of (super) nature. In the end, mankind must at least accept the power of the primordial world.<br /> <br /> We are not so far above the cavemen as we think we are.<br /> <br /> As for that reincarnation business, I've got words on that since I involved the possibility of it in my story, but that'll come later.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-14T13:05:51-07:00","id":847256,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/846958-how-does-a-human-become-a-beast?p=847245#post847245\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In real life, the answer is yes. We've seen it done, but it largely takes a lifetime.<br /> <br /> Does this mean a person can build the metaphysical infrastructure needed to become a Beast? The answer to that is <i>maaaaybe</i>, but you would need someone who knew what was going on, knew how to affect it within the limits of their mortality, had the desire to do it, and the dedication to do it. And all of that would probably still take a lifetime.<br /> <br /> So really, the answer's no. Maybe one in a millenium does it, and I can't see it benefiting them much in their old age, in fact it probably leads to them dying soon after that. Which is in someways appropriate to Beast's themes. Mankind is capable of great things, but it's not as capable as the forces of (super) nature. In the end, mankind must at least accept the power of the primordial world.<br /> <br /> We are not so far above the cavemen as we think we are.<br /> <br /> As for that reincarnation business, I've got words on that since I involved the possibility of it in my story, but that'll come later.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why do i have the Image of Medusa and Crona from Soul Eater in my Head from this?.....<br /> <br /> It Really shouldn't but that's what my head turns towards... In that case though it's someone else Shaping them into the &quot;Beast&quot;... breaking them in just the right way so they leave a Legacy Carved into someone else....<br /> <br /> Meh Don't know why....","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Light and Dark are two Sides of a Coin... Humanity is What Happens when it Lands on it's Edge.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3981-rickmanuk","name":"RickmanUK","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"533"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-14T13:12:22-07:00","id":847263,"title":"","content":"I still would largely say no","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-14T13:43:42-07:00","id":847282,"title":"","content":"There were two Beasts in a game I was playing a little while ago- one of them believed her Horror was utterly ancient, and was cast down by some mighty Atlantean mage or other, engineering her reincarnation over millennia. The player was planning on purchasing Mimir's Well in order to represent that accumulated ancient wisdom, but the player and the ST left it up in the air as to whether her backstory was true, or whether her Devouring had utterly broken her mind and the belief she was a reincarnated dragon was a delusion to hide her trauma. It was an <i>awesome </i>source of conflict, because while she played her Beast as a relatively balanced and mostly human creature, the other Beast was one with a young Horror, also in the shape of a dragon, that practically worshipped the ground she walked on and this younger Beast seemed a lot more unhinged- joyfully indulging her Hunger for Ruin.<br /> <br /> What ended up coming out as time went on was that the younger Beast was so enthusiastic mostly because she was almost always Low Satiety, and when she gained Satiety she mellowed out a bit and seemed a lot more disturbed by her own inhumanity than before- utterly crushed that the rest of the party saw her as a monster, and taking the teaching of lessons as a serious duty. The older Beast, who we previously thought was the more reasonable and human, turned out to just be acting, and when an opportunity to indulge her Hunger for Prey and merge with her Horror came up she relished it- unleashing a swathe of horrifying destruction without a care in the world for people getting hurt, and turning on my character (a Promethean) for <i>daring </i>to imply she was more human than she seemed and attempting to bolster feelings of unity, courage, and acceptance within the party by creative use of the Firebringer Transmutation.<br /> <br /> IC, the ST had some sort of antagonistic relationship between Primordial Dream and Divine Fire, and while the Transmutation had the desired effect on the younger Beast, who was Gorged at the time, it actually scorched the soul of the older one. Since both of them had the Dragonfire Atavism, the sudden inhumanity and violence from the older one had my character really, really nervous, and had the whole group questioning what we thought we knew about both Beasts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-14T15:30:17-07:00","id":847337,"title":"","content":"So If I wanted to make a human turning into Beast storyline with multiple characters...how would I go around it? It's not like a group of Kin travelling together only to be forced to ghoulhood/vampirism by their Sire. How would I go about this? <br /> <br /> And are there pictures of each of the Beasts? I'm kinda confused what all the species look like or if there is official splash of all the families.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11457-volke","name":"Volke","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11457_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"127"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-14T16:25:22-07:00","id":847384,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Volke</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/846958-how-does-a-human-become-a-beast?p=847337#post847337\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And are there pictures of each of the Beasts? I'm kinda confused what all the species look like or if there is official splash of all the families.</div> </div> </div> </div>The appearance of the horrors isn't really defined. They tend to follow themes though. A dragon anakim is going to be big, eshmaki dark and toothy, makara serpentine, namtaru horrendous, and ugallu strong eyes and wings.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3323-cmwatford","name":"cmwatford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3323_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"192"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-14T16:35:17-07:00","id":847387,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Volke</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/846958-how-does-a-human-become-a-beast?p=847337#post847337\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So If I wanted to make a human turning into Beast storyline with multiple characters...how would I go around it? It's not like a group of Kin travelling together only to be forced to ghoulhood/vampirism by their Sire. How would I go about this?<br /> <br /> And are there pictures of each of the Beasts? I'm kinda confused what all the species look like or if there is official splash of all the families.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you want more than the series of revelatory nightmares, consider appropriating Werewolf's growing intensity of spiritual events culminating a character's collapse of nightmare and reality into the ouroboros of being, the revelation that your dreams and your life are one and the same.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-14T16:42:37-07:00","id":847392,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Volke</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/846958-how-does-a-human-become-a-beast?p=847337#post847337\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So If I wanted to make a human turning into Beast storyline with multiple characters...how would I go around it? It's not like a group of Kin travelling together only to be forced to ghoulhood/vampirism by their Sire. How would I go about this?<br /> <br /> And are there pictures of each of the Beasts? I'm kinda confused what all the species look like or if there is official splash of all the families.</div> </div> </div> </div>To an extent you'd be dealing with people who have recurring nightmares. You might be able to spin that into prophetic insight via their nightmares/dreams to portray the sensitivity to primordial dream. Eventually you'd be building up to some incident where in the nightmares they either confront or are confronted by the monster from the nightmare and then there's the Devouring/Homecoming. <br /> <br /> As far as looks go. Beasts look like humans.One's Horror is a variable from individual to individual, but it only appears in the lair or as a kind of overshadowing that supernaturals see when a Beast uses and atavism. Families tend to have their archetypes, but which monster can fit into a family is really up for grabs. Like to give an example let's say you wanted your Horror to be represented by the scarab swarm from &quot;The Mummy.&quot; Now strictly speaking swarms and insects are usually a Namtaru thing, and certainly people are probably not going to argue that those bugs were pretty. On the other hand that swarm proceeded would just roll over in a massive amount and consume anything that couldn't escape it, which is so very Anakim. The Ugallu are normally winged flying monsters, but they're the nightmares of exposure. Thus why someone on the forum created a mirror monster thing that exposes all of a person's secrets. <br /> <br /> Your best bet is to figure out the Horror and the approach and then figure out how they handle things.From there you handle slot your Beast into what family it fits with and what type of feeding it does.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-14T16:57:21-07:00","id":847400,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>espritdecalmar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/846958-how-does-a-human-become-a-beast?p=847173#post847173\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's fair. I wonder if there are any Begotten who put the cart before the horse and think that their Horror is literally a specific monster from myth. Retreading Sacrosanct territory is probably unnecessary, but it could make for an interesting conflict, especially if an Apex (or Apex-aspiring) is involved.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Well when it comes down to it, the Beast's horror is just that; a horror. They embody a certain type of fear, but what form that fear takes can be just about anything.<br /> <br /> Giants being fear of powerlessness. When people think of Giants, they usually think of something huge and lumbering. That could include the traditional large human, a one eyed Cyclops, a bull headed Minotaur, a horned Oni, the hairy Yeti, an iron Golem. These are just ideas I came up with off the top of my head.<br /> <br /> The important thing is that the horror's appearance is symbolic of their fear. The details behind it's appearance are less important than the message. it conveys.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-14T17:08:29-07:00","id":847415,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Inquisitor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/846958-how-does-a-human-become-a-beast?p=847232#post847232\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Expanding this metaphor: Is there any way to carve out a cliff by oneself?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Of course is it, but it's not something ordinary people do. You don't just decide &quot;I'm going to become a monster today.&quot; It takes something to bring you to that point. A Beast is somebody who confronted their inner monster and merged with it. They are no longer human, they are something different.<br /> <br /> <br /> Anybody (meaning any human) can be embraced as a Vampire, undergo the first change as a Werewolf, awaken as a Mage, or be taken as a Changeling. But just because anybody can do it, doesn't mean everybody does. Circumstances in one's life bring them to that point and then events unfold from there.<br /> <br /> <br /> The concept behind the New World of Darkness is that you were raised as a human, you became something else, and now you have to deal with that. It's more about personal horror and moral choices than classic World of Darkness was.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 03-14-2016, 08:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-14T18:10:20-07:00","id":847442,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/846958-how-does-a-human-become-a-beast?p=847415#post847415\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anybody (meaning any human) can be embraced as a Vampire, undergo the first change as a Werewolf, awaken as a Mage, or be taken as a Changeling. But just because anybody can do it, doesn't mean everybody does. Circumstances in one's life bring them to that point and then events unfold from there.</div> </div> </div> </div>The thing Beast's themes kind of emphasize is less &quot;anybody can do it&quot; and more &quot;it can happen to anybody,&quot; and furthermore that &quot;anybody&quot; still tends to be dictated by the whims of fate and/or the many terrifying gods that populate the shadows of the setting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-14T18:54:29-07:00","id":847461,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/846958-how-does-a-human-become-a-beast?p=847442#post847442\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The thing Beast's themes kind of emphasize is less &quot;anybody can do it&quot; and more &quot;it can happen to anybody,&quot; and furthermore that &quot;anybody&quot; still tends to be dictated by the whims of fate and/or the many terrifying gods that populate the shadows of the setting.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Well yeah, that's kind of how Werewolves work too. Anybody has the potential to become a Werewolf, but actually provoking the First Change is a matter of fate, or being chosen by whatever cosmic forces govern the universe. Even then, I've been told that it is also possible to provoke a First Change by subjecting somebody to Lunacy, which means they can, in theory, convert people.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-14T19:19:01-07:00","id":847467,"title":"","content":"Alright I think I've begun to slowly understand it. Now Beasts survive through causing fears through their hungers like Ruin and Punishment, Correct? Or have I misunderstood the things beasts need to do to survive.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11457-volke","name":"Volke","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11457_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"127"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-14T20:29:16-07:00","id":847502,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Volke</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/846958-how-does-a-human-become-a-beast?p=847467#post847467\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Alright I think I've begun to slowly understand it. Now Beasts survive through causing fears through their hungers like Ruin and Punishment, Correct? Or have I misunderstood the things beasts need to do to survive.</div> </div> </div> </div>Beasts who haven't claimed the Incarnate Inheritance will gradually reach the point of dying in fairly short order if they don't get Satiety in some fashion, the most consistently available venue for which is their Hunger, yes. Beasts who explore Kinship will tend to have a few other options available to them through the use of Family Dinner's sympathetic feeding and possibly a few Kinship Nightmares they may develop, such as We Know All Your Secrets or Cursed Object.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-14T20:58:49-07:00","id":847522,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/846958-how-does-a-human-become-a-beast?p=847502#post847502\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Beasts who haven't claimed the Incarnate Inheritance will gradually reach the point of dying in fairly short order if they don't get Satiety in some fashion, the most consistently available venue for which is their Hunger, yes.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wasn't aware they could even reach the point of dying. I thought they just wandered into other peoples dreamscapes and feed there when they were too hungry.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-14T21:48:25-07:00","id":847536,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/846958-how-does-a-human-become-a-beast?p=847522#post847522\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wasn't aware they could even reach the point of dying. I thought they just wandered into other peoples dreamscapes and feed there when they were too hungry.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a resisted dice roll of two traits and there's a physical distance constraint.<br /> <br /> Also the death-spiral kicks in when you lose your last dot of Satiety, which is not strictly a time-based occurrence and makes the above a near-categorically disastrous thing to stake your sustenance on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{